{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -100 docs/DECISIONS-log.md | cat -n; rg -n 'D741|D745|D747' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t    1. T10 (S, Claude writer) F11: \"an estimated $750 billion\" recorded with qualifier \"none\". Both adjudicators upheld it. \"estimated\" is\n     2\t       not in the closed qualifier list, so the format forced \"none\". This is 1 affected figure of 251 source figures in the three writer\n     3\t       runs.\n     4\t    2. S has zero usable replies. Both writers state a data-center share of total capex (90%; 95–100%) that the passages do not size, and\n     5\t       the share decides the band.\n     6\t  - **E's Codex reply** is now \"not supported\": its 15% cut from the guided floor decides the band. This is the same weakness.\n     7\t- **Council round 59** (`codex-r59.md`) chose a targeted $0 test, (c), over Claude's lean to go to Alex for the paid re-send, (b):\n     8\t  - Going straight to the paid re-send would measure the known weakness in gpt-6-luna without the request saying what a supported size\n     9\t    is.\n    10\t  - Skipping a clean result needs Alex to change the registered sequence anyway.\n    11\t  - Claude agrees: the weakness is unsupported precision in a number that decides the rung, which is the goal's own failure (D725).\n    12\t- **Proposed test (for Alex to authorize):**\n    13\t  1. Add \"estimated\" to the qualifier list, and show readers the allowed values. Prove it on the saved replies, with a case and a\n    14\t     mutant.\n    15\t  2. Add one clarification to the existing instruction: when a deduction or cut decides the band, show the evidence for its size or a\n    16\t     bound the passages support that justifies the band; if neither, answer unresolved.\n    17\t  3. Test on S and on one stored case where the passages do support a narrower figure.\n    18\t  4. Before the test, Alex rules whether a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n    19\t  - Falsifier: a fresh S answer still picks a band on an unsupported share, or the supported case is withheld.\n    20\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-23):\n    21\t  - to \"怎么走？\": \"批准针对性小测 (推荐)\". The other options were \"不小测，直接议花钱重发\" and \"先停在这里\".\n    22\t  - to whether a justified \"无法判断\" counts: \"算合格 (推荐)\". The other option was \"不算\".\n    23\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n    24\t  1. Run the targeted $0 test.\n    25\t  2. An unresolved answer whose reason shows the passages cannot settle the rung counts as a usable answer.\n    26\t- **Council round 60** (`codex-r60.md`) set the wording and the registration (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D745]):\n    27\t  - Rung-deciding shares, deductions and discounts must show their passage support or a justifying bound, else unresolved.\n    28\t  - The default discount is made subject to that rule.\n    29\t  - The three controls are the saved E 15% cut, a vague P-v8 unresolved answer and a justified S unresolved answer (expected no, no,\n    30\t    yes).\n    31\t  - Pass: every S and E reply settled yes on a forecast or its reason; both P-v8 replies settled yes on a forecast. A support split\n    32\t    is inconclusive.\n    33\t\n    34\t## D746 · 2026-11-23 · The D745 targeted test fails on E's unsized cut; S splits on how far an indirect comparison can support a forecast; council 61–61b: one general question to Alex, then a $0 stored-answer re-read; the paid re-send stays on hold\n    35\t\n    36\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/`,\n    37\t  `TALLY.json`):\n    38\t  - **FAIL on a registered line.** E's Codex reply (rung 3, $36B) realises 90% of the $40B reference and itself says \"the passages\n    39\t    give no order sizes or shipment pace\". Both first readers marked it not supported.\n    40\t  - **Four splits, all along model family** (8 of 8 adjudicator votes went with their own family): S Claude (98% share), S Codex ($25B\n    41\t    deduction), E Claude (1.8x with a 90% Vera share) and the justified-unresolved S control.\n    42\t  - **The rest:**\n    43\t    - P-v8: 2 of 2 supported;\n    44\t    - the unsupported-cut and vague-unresolved controls read as expected;\n    45\t    - no refusal, no defect;\n    46\t    - 0 of 6 replies withheld.\n    47\t  - **One construction change, disclosed.** The justified-unresolved control was rebuilt on the third run's S Codex reply, because the\n    48\t    S Claude reply is refused by the current code (S1). Its reason text is unchanged.\n    49\t- **Council rounds 61 and 61b** (`claude-r61.md`, `codex-r61.md`, `codex-r61b.md`) reached consensus:\n    50\t  - **The FAIL stands.** Resolving every split would still leave E's Codex reply failed.\n    51\t  - **Two problems.**\n    52\t    1. **The reading standard is not settled.** The open point is how far a related figure can support a forecast when the passages do\n    53\t       not measure the asked quantity on the deciding side.\n    54\t       - S has split this way in three readings: \"more than $730B on AI infrastructure\" for the same four companies, as a floor for\n    55\t         their data-center spending.\n    56\t       - E Claude's bracket fails on its own assumptions ($20B × 1.5 × 90% = $27B, rung 4). That point is arithmetic.\n    57\t       - D741 ruling 3 still requires a stated deduction or a supported bound. The threshold for \"supported\" when the support is an\n    58\t         indirect comparison is Alex's to set.\n    59\t    2. **Writers size a risk without evidence.** 3 of 4 E replies across two runs carry a disputed cut or share, and D745's sentence\n    60\t       did not stop it.\n    61\t  - **Corrections.**\n    62\t    - Claude withdrew two reasons for the lean. D725 does not promise that code catches every invented figure. AGENTS §8's \"no data to\n    63\t      verify\" concerns outcomes after the fact.\n    64\t    - The result page was corrected in three places: U05 had two first readers; unresolved singletons are published and inspected; the\n    65\t      paid S asks about CY2027.\n    66\t    - Whether a paid STOP is predictable: it is a conditional risk, not a measured rate (Codex; Claude agrees).\n    67\t  - **The recommendation.** Ask Alex one general question (below), with a lean to allow the forecast when the answer explains why the\n    68\t    comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked, and why, under its own assumptions, that side of the line\n    69\t    is more likely.\n    70\t  - **The one test after his ruling.** A $0 blinded re-read of nine stored answers under his words, added to the shared definitions:\n    71\t    - the answers: U01–U06, U08, the third run's T10 (for its spending argument only), and T15 (the accepted E bracket);\n    72\t    - fresh readers, one per family;\n    73\t    - what his choice implies for each answer is recorded before reading.\n    74\t    - It moves on to a writer repair only if both families apply his words alike. A continuing split leaves the publication question\n    75\t      open in practice. A clean re-read does not turn D745 into a pass.\n    76\t  - **The paid re-send stays on hold** until an E writer repair passes a clean $0 test. The proposed repair: the writer chooses between\n    77\t    a forecast and \"can't tell\" before it assigns a discount, naming what makes one side more likely under its own assumptions. It is a\n    78\t    new arm and goes to council before any send. Publishing management's figure whenever it sits on a cutoff would change the product,\n    79\t    and needs Alex's own decision.\n    80\t- **The question to Alex** (pending): \"资料没直接给出所问的数。用一个相关数字作比较，能解释为什么结果更可能在线的这一边，但另一边仍有可能。这时可以发布预测，还是要等到能从资料算出结果落在线的哪一边？\"\n    81\t- **Not done.** Nothing was paid. Nothing was tuned on the 36 stored answers. The request was not changed after the registration.\n    82\t\n    83\t## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n    84\t\n    85\t- **The question** (after D746): \"资料没直接给出题目问的那个数，只能拿一个相关的数字来比。比如问四大云厂商今年的数据中心开支能不能过 7000 亿，资料只说“这四家 AI 基础设施开支超过 7300 亿”。这种比较能说明结果更可能落在线的某一边，但另一边也还有可能。这时系统可以发布预测吗，还是要等资料能直接算出落在哪边？\"\n    86\t  - Options:\n    87\t    - \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\": the answer must explain why the comparison applies to the companies, the year and the quantity\n    88\t      asked, and why, under its own assumptions, that side is more likely; an answer that cannot explain it is not supported;\n    89\t    - \"先说“还判断不了”\";\n    90\t    - \"先停在这里\".\n    91\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\".\n    92\t- **Decided (Alex).** When the passages do not give the asked quantity, a forecast may rest on a related figure. It is supported\n    93\t  only when the answer explains two things: why the comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked; and why,\n    94\t  under the answer's own stated assumptions, the chosen side of the line is more likely. An answer that cannot explain this is not\n    95\t  supported.\n    96\t  - D741 ruling 3 still holds: a total used for a narrower quantity states the deduction as its own figure, or gives a supported\n    97\t    bound.\n    98\t  - D745's ruling still holds: a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n    99\t- **Next (D746).** The ruling's words go into the shared reader definitions (`blind_rules.py`). Then one $0 blinded re-read of nine\n   100\t  stored answers, registered with its expected readings and reviewed by the council before any packet is read.\n11346:## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n11383:      O's rung, and D741 ruling 2 does not settle it.\n11397:- **Decided (council, under Alex's \"那你自己持续迭代\" and D741 ruling 1):**\n11484:## D745 · 2026-11-23 · The D744 re-read calibrates the readers but stops on a qualifier-list gap and on S's unsupported share; council 59 recommends a targeted $0 test of one clarification, for Alex to authorize\n11516:- **Council round 60** (`codex-r60.md`) set the wording and the registration (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D745]):\n11524:## D746 · 2026-11-23 · The D745 targeted test fails on E's unsized cut; S splits on how far an indirect comparison can support a forecast; council 61–61b: one general question to Alex, then a $0 stored-answer re-read; the paid re-send stays on hold\n11547:       - D741 ruling 3 still requires a stated deduction or a supported bound. The threshold for \"supported\" when the support is an\n11549:    2. **Writers size a risk without evidence.** 3 of 4 E replies across two runs carry a disputed cut or share, and D745's sentence\n11565:      open in practice. A clean re-read does not turn D745 into a pass.\n11573:## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n11586:  - D741 ruling 3 still holds: a total used for a narrower quantity states the deduction as its own figure, or gives a supported\n11588:  - D745's ruling still holds: a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
